{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-1-5","title":"1 Crónicas 1:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Introducción al libro - 1 Crónicas Lea el primer capítulo de 1 Crónicas Los dos libros de Crónicas (como los dos libros de Reyes) son sólo un libro en el canon judío. Juntos cubren el período desde la muerte de Saúl hasta los cautiverios. Probablemente fueron escritos durante el cautiverio babilónico y se distinguen de los dos libros de los Reyes por un relato más completo de Judá y por la omisión de muchos detalles. La bendición del pueblo terrenal de Dios en relación con la monarquía davídica es probablemente el significado típico de estos libros. Primera de Crónicas consta de tres partes: Genealogías oficiales, 1:1-9:44. Desde la muerte de Saúl hasta el ascenso de David, 10:1-12:24. Desde el ascenso de David hasta su muerte, 13:1-29:30. Excluyendo las genealogías (Capítulos 1-9), los acontecimientos registrados en Primeras Crónicas cubren un período de 41 años (Ussher). Magog Génesis 10:2; Ezequiel 38:2; 39:6; Apocalipsis 20:8. (véase Scofield &quot;Ezequiel 38:2&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-1-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-2-13","title":"1 Crónicas 2:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Shimma o Shammah, 1 Samuel 16:9.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-2-13","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-2-54","title":"1 Crónicas 2:54","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":54,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":54},"content":"<p>Ataroth O, Ataritas, o, coronas de la casa de Joab.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-2-54","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-3-2","title":"1 Crónicas 3:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Absalón (véase Scofield &quot;2 Samuel 13:37&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-3-2","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-5-6","title":"1 Crónicas 5:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Tilgathpilneser O, Tiglathpileser, 2 Reyes 15:29; 16:7.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-5-6","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-5-20","title":"1 Crónicas 5:20","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>confianza (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 2:12&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-5-20","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-6-68","title":"1 Crónicas 6:68","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":68,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":68},"content":"<p>Jokmeam Ver Josué 21:22-35 donde muchas de estas ciudades tienen otros nombres:</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-6-68","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-7-12","title":"1 Crónicas 7:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Shupim Shufam y Hufam. Números 26:39.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-7-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-7-28","title":"1 Crónicas 7:28","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Narran Naarath, Josué 16:7.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-7-28","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-9-26","title":"1 Crónicas 9:26","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>cámaras, es decir, almacenes.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-9-26","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-9-32","title":"1 Crónicas 9:32","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>pan de la proposición (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 25:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-9-32","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-9-41","title":"1 Crónicas 9:41","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>y Acaz agregado de 1 Crónicas 8:35.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-9-41","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-11-5","title":"1 Crónicas 11:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>castillo de Sión Heb. castillo. (1) Sión, la antigua fortaleza jebusea, es la eminencia suroeste de Jerusalén, llamada en las Escrituras la ciudad de David y asociada con la realeza davídica tanto histórica como proféticamente 1 Crónicas 11:7; Salmo 2:6; Isaías 2:3. La palabra se usa a menudo para toda la ciudad de Jerusalén considerada como la ciudad de Dios Salmo 48:2,3 especialmente en pasajes que se refieren a la futura era del reino; Isaías 1:27; 2:3; 4:1-6; Joel 3:16; Zacarías 1:16,17; 8:3-8; Romanos 11:26. En Hebreos 12:22 la palabra se usa simbólicamente del cielo. (2) En Deuteronomio 4:48 se le da el nombre a una proyección o pico del monte Hermón.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-11-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-12-15","title":"1 Crónicas 12:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>primer mes, es decir, abril.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-12-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-13-11","title":"1 Crónicas 13:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":13,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":13,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Perezuzza, es decir, la infracción de Uzza.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-13-11","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-16-4","title":"1 Crónicas 16:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>registro Ver títulos de los Salmos 38 y 70.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-16-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-16-16","title":"1 Crónicas 16:16","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Abraham (véase Scofield &quot;Génesis 15:18&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-16-16","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-16-25","title":"1 Crónicas 16:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>temido (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-16-25","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-16-37","title":"1 Crónicas 16:37","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>Se entenderá que el antiguo tabernáculo estaba ahora dividido; el arca fue llevada a &quot;Sión&quot;. (véase Scofield &quot;1 Crónicas 11:5&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-16-37","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-18-8","title":"1 Crónicas 18:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Tibhat llamado Betah y Berothai. 2 Samuel 8:8.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-18-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-18-12","title":"1 Crónicas 18:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Abisai Sobrino de David, hermano de Joab. 2 Samuel 23:18; 1 Crónicas 2:16.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-18-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-20-1","title":"1 Crónicas 20:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>David Aquí debe leerse 2 Samuel 11:2-12:25; Salmo 51:1-19.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-20-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-4","title":"1 Crónicas 21:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>partió Aquí debe leer 2 Samuel 24:4-9.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-5","title":"1 Crónicas 21:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>fueron mil Cf. (véase Scofield &quot;2 Samuel 24:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-12","title":"1 Crónicas 21:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Margen (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-15","title":"1 Crónicas 21:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>ángel (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-18","title":"1 Crónicas 21:18","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>ángel (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-18","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-20","title":"1 Crónicas 21:20","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>ángel (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-20","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-25","title":"1 Crónicas 21:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>seiscientos siclos de oro Se ha imaginado una discrepancia en las dos cuentas, 2 Samuel 24:24; 1 Crónicas 21:25; 2 Samuel 24:24 registra el precio de la era (heb. goren); 1 Crónicas 21:25 del lugar (heb. magom, lit. &quot;hogar&quot;, 1 Samuel 2:20) misma palabra o área en la que luego se construyó el gran templo, con sus espaciosos patios. 2 Crónicas 3:1. David dio cincuenta siclos de plata por el &quot;goren&quot;; seiscientos siclos de oro para el &quot;magom&quot;.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-25","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-21-27","title":"1 Crónicas 21:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>ángel (véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 1:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-21-27","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-23-22","title":"1 Crónicas 23:22","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>hermanos, es decir, primos.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-23-22","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-23-28","title":"1 Crónicas 23:28","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>oficio, es decir, su nuevo oficio, ya que su oficio anterior de llevar el tabernáculo terminó.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-23-28","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-23-29","title":"1 Crónicas 23:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>pan de la proposición (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 25:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-23-29","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-2","title":"1 Crónicas 27:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>primer mes, es decir, abril; 1 Crónicas 27:3.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-2","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-4","title":"1 Crónicas 27:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>segundo mes, es decir, mayo.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-5","title":"1 Crónicas 27:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>tercer mes, es decir, junio.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-7","title":"1 Crónicas 27:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>cuarto mes, es decir, julio.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-7","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-8","title":"1 Crónicas 27:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>quinto mes, es decir, agosto.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-9","title":"1 Crónicas 27:9","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>sexto mes, es decir, septiembre.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-9","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-10","title":"1 Crónicas 27:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>séptimo mes, es decir, octubre.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-10","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-11","title":"1 Crónicas 27:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>octavo mes, es decir, noviembre.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-11","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-12","title":"1 Crónicas 27:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>noveno mes, es decir, diciembre.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-13","title":"1 Crónicas 27:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>décimo mes, es decir, enero.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-13","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-14","title":"1 Crónicas 27:14","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>undécimo mes, es decir, febrero.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-14","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-27-15","title":"1 Crónicas 27:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>duodécimo mes, es decir, marzo.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-27-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-28-16","title":"1 Crónicas 28:16","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>pan de la proposición (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 25:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-28-16","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-29-10","title":"1 Crónicas 29:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>bendito Note el orden: 1 Crónicas 29:3-8, dar, 1 Crónicas 29:9, gozo, 1 Crónicas 29:10, bendición, 1 Crónicas 29:11-19, oración, 1 Crónicas 29:20, adoración:</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-29-10","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-1ch-29-29","title":"1 Crónicas 29:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>libro de Estos libros han perecido.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-1ch-29-29","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}}]}
